      "question": "Find the official Node.js documentation: does fs.readFile support AbortSignal, and what is the cancellation limitation?\nFind the official Node.js documentation: when are worker_threads useful for CPU-intensive work versus asynchronous I/O?",
      "elapsedMs": 24927,
      "ok": true,
      "body": "- **`fs.readFile()` supports `AbortSignal`.** Pass it as `options.signal`. If an ongoing read is aborted, the callback receives an `AbortError`. The limitation is that cancellation stops `fs.readFile()`’s internal buffering; it does **not** abort individual operating-system requests. [Node.js file-system documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/fs.html#fsreadfilepath-options-callback)\n- **`worker_threads` are useful for CPU-intensive JavaScript work.** They offer little benefit for I/O-intensive work because Node.js’s built-in asynchronous I/O operations are more efficient. [Node.js worker-threads documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/worker_threads.html#worker-threads)",
